# Copy to .env.local and fill in. NEVER commit real secrets.
#
# A fresh local install needs NONE of this up front (S-52): the launcher
# generates AUTH_SECRET itself, sign-in uses a GitHub device code with no
# OAuth app, the first sign-in claims ALLOWED_LOGINS, and provider keys can
# be pasted in Settings. Everything below is for overriding those defaults —
# and for hosted deployments, which need the AUTH_* values set explicitly.

# Auth.js session secret — generated on first run locally. Generate by hand
# with:  npx auth secret   (or: openssl rand -base64 33)
AUTH_SECRET=

# OPTIONAL locally (device-code sign-in needs neither) — REQUIRED hosted.
# Your own GitHub OAuth App: github.com → Settings → Developer settings → OAuth Apps
#   Homepage URL:               http://localhost:4300   (or your hosted URL)
#   Authorization callback URL: http://localhost:4300/api/auth/callback/github
# With AUTH_GITHUB_SECRET set, sign-in uses the classic web redirect. Setting
# only AUTH_GITHUB_ID switches the device flow to your app's client id.
AUTH_GITHUB_ID=
AUTH_GITHUB_SECRET=

# Anthropic API key — https://console.anthropic.com/ (or paste in Settings)
ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=

# Comma-separated GitHub usernames allowed to sign in.
# Empty on a LOCAL install: the first device-code sign-in claims it (E-10.d).
# Non-empty (and always on hosted): FAIL-CLOSED — only listed accounts get in.
ALLOWED_LOGINS=

# Optional: override the chat model id. Must be one of the ids in config/models.json
# and one your ANTHROPIC_API_KEY can access.
# IDEA_CHAT_MODEL=claude-sonnet-5

# Optional: keys for the other bundled providers (config/models.json).
# A model whose provider has no key is simply never routed to.
# OPENAI_API_KEY=
# GEMINI_API_KEY=
# MOONSHOT_API_KEY=
# DASHSCOPE_API_KEY=

# Hosted mode (FR-15, docs/architecture/12-hosted-mode.md). Never needed on a
# machine you own. On Vercel it turns on automatically (VERCEL=1); IDEA_HOSTED=1
# forces it on any other serverless host. Hosted mode disables everything
# disk-bound and expects each signed-in user to bring their own provider keys.
# IDEA_HOSTED=1

# Site-only mode (S-52): the deployment is a plain product website — the
# homepage is the download page, and chat/settings/sign-in all redirect home.
# Remove the var (and redeploy) to bring the hosted console back.
# IDEA_SITE_ONLY=1

# Hosted store (S-51) — saved chats + per-user settings on a hosted deployment.
# Supabase project → Settings → API. Run supabase/schema.sql once in the SQL
# editor first. Use the secret key (sb_secret_…); the legacy service_role JWT
# also works. Without these, hosted chats are simply unsaved. Never needed
# locally — conversations live in each project's repo there.
# SUPABASE_URL=
# SUPABASE_SECRET_KEY=
